.TH WORDCOUNT 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
wordCount \- count newlines, words, and characters in a file stream
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <myfilefunctions.h>

int wordCount(FILE *file, int *lines, int *words, int *chars);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wordCount
reads from the current position of
.I file
until end-of-file. It stores the number of newline characters in
.IR lines ,
whitespace-separated words in
.IR words ,
and bytes read in
.IR chars .
Each output count is reset to zero before reading. A final line without
a newline does not increase the line count.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success and -1 for a NULL argument or stream read error.
